The OIDC path does not check the answer of the token endpoint.

lib/WWW/Authentik/OIDC.pm:487 returns ->{data} // {} from _token_call, without looking at the status or at the form of the answer. The same repository checks the 3xx on the API path (lib/WWW/Authentik/API.pm:161-167), the OIDC path does not. The cause is in lib/WWW/Authentik/Role/HTTP.pm:94: read_response delivers a result for every status below 400.

Failure case: the token endpoint answers 302 (a redirect from http to https, a login portal in front of it). client_credentials_token, refresh_token, exchange_authorization_code and device_token deliver {} without an exception. The caller sends Authorization: Bearer without a token and sees later "verify_token needs a token" instead of "the token endpoint has redirected".

Decide: _token_call raises a WWW::Authentik::Error::API with method, path and status when the status is 300 or above, or when the data is no token hash.

The test that holds this down must be red against the old lib/ and fail as a failed expectation, not as a die.

